{
 "_source": "Phantasie III, DOS SSI 1988 (reverse-engineering/dos/phantasie3/extracted/, FORMAT.md): INITARMS.DAT rows 0..17 x 181 B [C] (FORMAT.md section 9.3); price index DS:0x10fc + 2 * town [C] bytes (extent [~]); names = master string 111 + town [C]",
 "_layout": "stock[id] for item id 0..180 (stock[0] is always 0; the file's byte 0 is 'kinds', the number of ids with a non-zero count, checked here). Row 0 is unused; 15..17 (the plane towns) stock nothing. Counts of 200 / 99 / 77 on potions and scrolls = plenty. DOS never restocks; the remaster's default re-rolls weapons and potions on each town entry by Apple II's rule (D3-033, rule-tables.json armory_restock).",
 "_notes": [
  "id = the town number (FAR:0xdd98; 1 Pendragon .. 14 Sciattica, 15 Light, 16 Dark, 17 Death). The INITARMS row 0 is unused and left out.",
  "plane: the plane the town is on (root 0x1e18 picks the map by town: 15 Light, 16 Dark, 17 Netherworld) [C] (planes.md section 2). III has no TRANSPORTATION list (spell 54 offers towns 1-14, town.md section 8) and no I-style restock list (the restock pool is in rule-tables.json armory_restock, D3-033); the town square is in overworld.json places.",
  "Price: value * price_index / 100 (armory root 0x0f22, FORMAT.md section 4.1) [~]; training gold uses the same index (training.md section 3)."
